From 567e1c5ea7909536101323917e231b6a29a2071b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zelan Zou <zelan.zou@nxp.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw/xen: add missing xen_mr_is_grants() stub

hw/virtio/vhost.c is compiled unconditionally whenever vhost support is
enabled (vhost_user/vhost_kernel/vhost_vdpa default to 'auto' and
auto-enable on a Linux build host). vhost_section() in that file calls
xen_mr_is_grants(), guarded only at run time by xen_enabled().

When QEMU is built without CONFIG_XEN, hw/xen/xen-hvm-common.c (which
provides the real xen_mr_is_grants()) is not built; instead xen_stubs.c
is linked in. xen_stubs.c provides stubs for the other xen entry points
referenced from generic code (xen_mr_is_memory(), xen_ram_alloc(), ...)
but is missing a stub for xen_mr_is_grants(), leading to:

  undefined reference to `xen_mr_is_grants'

when linking e.g. qemu-system-arm in a non-xen configuration (observed
with nativesdk-qemu). Add the missing stub, matching the existing
xen_mr_is_memory() stub.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Zelan Zou <zelan.zou@nxp.com>
---
 hw/xen/xen_stubs.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/xen/xen_stubs.c b/hw/xen/xen_stubs.c
index 5e565df392..9420989805 100644
--- a/hw/xen/xen_stubs.c
+++ b/hw/xen/xen_stubs.c
@@ -29,6 +29,11 @@ bool xen_mr_is_memory(MemoryRegion *mr)
     g_assert_not_reached();
 }
 
+bool xen_mr_is_grants(MemoryRegion *mr)
+{
+    g_assert_not_reached();
+}
+
 void xen_invalidate_map_cache_entry(uint8_t *buffer)
 {
     g_assert_not_reached();
-- 
